{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe plan-review gate is reached through three surfaces: the CLI (`rebar review-plan`, handler `_review_plan` in `src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py:300`, parser `build_review_plan` in `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/llm.py`), the library (`rebar.llm.review_plan`, which already takes `engine` since [rebar:skilled-cepevorous-naga]), and the MCP tools `review_plan` and `review_plan_start` (`src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py`). Today only `[verify] plan_review_engine` selects the engine on the CLI and MCP paths, so an operator cannot run one ticket under both engines without editing config, and the MCP dedup key (`_plan_review_variant`, `_mcp_llm.py:88`) ignores the engine: a pipeline start and an agentic start on one ticket would attach to the same job.\n\n## Approach\n\nThread one optional `engine` argument down the existing call chains into `review_plan`. Precedence stays as ADR 0123 fixed it and `plan_review.resolve_plan_review_engine` implements: explicit argument, then `[verify] plan_review_engine`, then `\"pipeline\"`. No new config key or env var.\n\n- **CLI:** `build_review_plan` adds `--engine {pipeline,agentic}` (default None = config), and `_review_plan` passes `engine=args.engine` to `llm.review_plan`. `src/rebar/_cli/help/review-plan.txt` is regenerated with `scripts/gen_cli_help.py`, and its drift test (`tests/unit/test_gen_cli_help.py`) passes.\n- **MCP:** `review_plan` and `review_plan_start` gain `engine: str | None = None`, which `_review_plan_body` passes to `rebar.llm.review_plan`. `_plan_review_variant(ticket_id, source, engine)` resolves the engine first, through `resolve_plan_review_engine` against the server's config, and appends `;engine=<resolved>` to the key. Concurrent same-ticket starts under one engine still share a job; a pipeline start and an agentic start are distinct jobs. An explicit unknown value raises `ConfigError` from that resolution, before any job is created or LLM call made. Gate admission (`gate_admission`, ADR 0112) runs inside `review_plan`, so `GATE_CONGESTED` behaves identically for both engines. `verify_completion*` tools are unchanged.\n- **Docs:** `docs/mcp-reference.md` is regenerated with `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py` (it renders tool signatures), and `docs/plan-review-gate.md` gains a short \"Choosing the engine\" note naming the flag, the MCP parameter and the precedence.\n\nPassing one argument down the existing chain is the least change that gives every surface the switch; the library already has it.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/llm.py (flag)\n- src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py (pass engine)\n- src/rebar/_cli/help/review-plan.txt (regenerated)\n- src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py (tool parameters, body, dedup variant)\n- docs/mcp-reference.md (regenerated), docs/plan-review-gate.md\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review_engine_surfaces.py (new)\n\n## Testing\n\nAll offline with a counting FakeRunner (agent findings `[]`, so an agentic run PASSes) in a temp repo.\n\n- CLI: `rebar review-plan <id> --engine agentic -o json` returns `coverage.engine == \"agentic\"`; without the flag the configured default (pipeline) applies and coverage has no `engine`; `--engine bogus` exits 2 with an argparse error.\n- MCP sync: `review_plan(ticket_id, engine=\"agentic\")` returns the agentic verdict; `engine=\"bogus\"` raises `ConfigError` with zero runner calls.\n- MCP async: `review_plan_start(..., engine=\"agentic\")` then polling `gate_status(job_id)` to `passed` and `plan_review_status` to `certified`.\n- Dedup key: `_plan_review_variant` differs between `engine=\"pipeline\"` and `engine=\"agentic\"`, is equal for `None` and the configured default, and two concurrent same-engine `review_plan_start` calls return one `job_id`.\n- Congestion: with `gate_admission` refusing (`GateCongestedError`, an `LLMError`), the MCP sync tool returns the same `_structured_llm_failure` payload under both engines, and the CLI exits 11 under both.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The CLI flag, the MCP sync parameter and the async start/poll path each run the selected engine, pinned by `tests/unit/test_plan_review_engine_surfaces.py`.\n- [ ] Different engines get different dedup keys, same-engine starts share a job, and `GATE_CONGESTED` is unchanged, pinned by the same file.\n- [ ] `python scripts/gen_cli_help.py --check` and `python scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py --check` exit 0.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794459710457349622,"uuid":"1d55f359-bf7d-4f11-b081-fb2689ba0054"}